  m_text: Lerion is a traditional Philippine folk dance that captures the essence
    of rural life and natural beauty. Discovered in Parang, Marikina by the late
    Francisca Reyes Aquino and Simeona Chanyungco in the early 1950s, this dance
    reflects the harmonious relationship between villagers and their environment.
