    m_HorizontalOverflow: 0
    m_VerticalOverflow: 0
    m_LineSpacing: 1
  m_Text: "Spanish Influence: Introduced by Spanish settlers, Cari\xF1osa incorporates
    movements from Spanish courtship dances such as the bolero and jarabe tapatio.
    This fusion highlights the lasting impact of Spanish colonization on Philippine
    culture.\n\nRegional Variations: The Cari\xF1osa features regional adaptations
    across the Philippines. For instance, in the Bicol region, performers use handkerchiefs
    and exhibit distinct dance steps, showcasing local interpretations of this timeless
    dance."
